hello everyone and a happy new year as  many of you might know over december of  2021 toy animation claimed and blocked  over 150 of my videos this translates to  over three years worth of work being  removed from my channel that both myself  and my team worked hard to create  following those events i tried  everything from reaching out to youtube  support specifically to making videos  addressing it explicitly with all of you  guys helping to amplify my voice thank  you again by the way as it is because of  you that i have good and interesting  news to give today a lot has happened  since i last addressed this scenario  back in mid-december so i will be  filling you all in on everything that  has happened since and let me tell you a  lot has happened some really weird some  really good and a lot that i didn't even  know about as usual i will try to keep  this as brief as i can in mid-december i  released a video stating that i would be  stepping away from this entire situation  a lot of you found this abrupt and it  was however i assure you that it wasn't  a decision made for any other reason  than those stated in the video the  circumstances surrounding my videos  being taken down weren't the only things  that i had to contend with that month  i'm eager to share with you all the  details of my professional troubles  however i don't want to get into the  personal stressors that existed during  that time just know that they were a  large contributing factor that forced me  to take a step back  now onto some new stuff  following my last upload addressing this  situation on december 11th the very next  day on december 12th someone high up at  youtube who had requested i keep their  identity withheld reached out to me  personally on discord asking if they  could hop on a call with me from this  point on i will be referring to this  person as quote my youtube contact or  contact i immediately hopped onto this  call with the youtube contact and right  away they accepted responsibility for  this not being escalated sooner i had in  the past reached out to numerous youtube  support personnel through the proper  channels all to know success and to tons  of stress the youtube contact expressed  that this should never have been left  unanswered as long as it was and i'm not  gonna lie hearing a human voice that  felt both sincerely eager to help and  understanding of this impossible  situation felt like a weight lifted off  my shoulders and that's when they gave  me some information concerning the  situation i was not aware of my first  experience with this whole toei  situation began when i first received  those copyright notices via email  however my contact informed me that  there was much more to that story than  what happened after i received those  copyright emails firstly prior to any  email being sent to me toy animation  sent youtube directly over 150 takedown  notices these are requests to youtube  not to block my content but to delete  them off of my channel which would lead  to strikes right off the bat and likely  would result in the termination of my  account and that's bad but this is where  i want to give youtube some credit in  response to this request youtube as per  their policy did not remove the videos  but rather requested toei to confirm  that they had considered exceptions to  copyright such as fair use and fair  dealing in other words youtube looked at  my content and felt that the videos  might qualify for such an exception  courts have decided that copyright  owners must consider fair use before  they send a takedown and so they pass  the ball back to toei to provide further  reasoning and this is where this gets  interesting in response to this toei  broke youtube's policy and instead of  responding with a justification for  their takedown notices per youtube's  request they instead use their own tools  behind youtube's back to manually claim  and block each and every one of the over  150 videos in my catalogue of content  effectively achieving the same result  minus the takedown of my channel this is  what resulted in the 150 emails i  received alerting to me of this in the  first place so in short toei explicitly  broke the rules in this instance it is  important however at this time to point  out that had toei provided an argument  that the videos were infringing under  japanese law youtube would have likely  honored their removal removed the videos  worldwide and potentially struck out my  channel youtube's justification for  following this notice and take down  process ultimately boils down to youtube  wanting to retain their safe harbor  status if they lost this status they  would be picking aside and thus opened  themselves up to countless lawsuits from  all angles but in this instance toei  broke the rules of youtube's copyright  policy which made every single one of  those copyright claims and blocks that  toei filed against me  null and void  and this might sound great and following  this conversation over the days that  followed i technically had all of my  videos back under my control and  technically fully monetizable but as my  contact informed me we were far from out  of the woods yet they said that if i  were to put all the videos back up as  they were i would run a massive risk of  opening myself up to the exact same  thing happening again and perhaps this  time toei would provide that  justification they needed last time if  they did this then my videos would be  deleted and perhaps my channel too fair  use is a defense that makes sense in  most countries and certainly the ones i  broadcast to specifically however the  japanese interpretation of these  exceptions is less robust than most of  the rest of the world which is why i  made all of the claimed videos private  so that i could buy time to understand  my options over the next week my contact  jumped into a number of different  meetings and indirect correspondence  with the japanese youtube  representatives communicating with toei  to try and mediate some sort of  understanding initially they wanted to  see if it was possible to establish a  meeting between myself and a rep from  toei however the idea was quickly  discarded for a number of reasons  following this youtube asked  toyanimation to review all of my videos  they requested takedowns for since some  of them clearly didn't use any of their  footage and this is when something  incredibly surprising and concerning  occurred toei obliged and made a list of  86 videos that they said should stay  down with the implication being anything  that wasn't on this list could go back  up my contact shared this list with me  and asked me to review it and what i  found was honestly baffling contained in  this list were frankly the most  arbitrary assortment of videos i had  ever seen it honestly appeared as though  someone chose videos at random as if  chucking darts at a dartboard for  example my first video in which i drew  characters in a particular style was  included on this bad video list but the  second episode which had literally the  exact same style format and volume of  content wasn't to add to the confusion  some parts of my dragon ball review  series were requested to be taken down  while others which were part of that  same review series were not and to keep  in mind these are videos that were  edited in the exact same fashion as the  part which wasn't allowed the same is  true for my one piece series some of it  was to be taken down while others  weren't and as i continued reading this  list provided by toy animation i became  more and more confused so much so that i  wrote up a four-page document expressing  my concerns and the issues i saw with it  in the interest of transparency i will  read my closing statements from that  document where i reviewed the  aforementioned list to give you all a  taste of where my head was at the time i  was not happy  quote this is where i am going to stop  going through these videos simply put  either they're all okay or they're not  my most charitable reading of these  decisions is that those at toy animation  tasked with this assignment quite  literally have no excuse at this point  for producing such an incoherent and  incomprehensible list of unacceptable  and acceptable videos toei have in their  very own list demonstrated that they do  not understand the task or rules that  they are asking others to abide by this  list is rife with contradictions and  incomprehensible choices that i  personally find as both a head of a  household and a company deeply  disturbing if toei doesn't know the  rules of their own game that how can  they possibly justify this behavior  end quote and that's about as far as the  situation got before the holiday break  both in japan and america and there  wasn't any more to report until the  first week of january 2022  following this my youtube contact held  meetings with numerous other youtube  personnel trying to find some solution  to this existing issue i should make it  known at this time that i have never  spoken to toy animation nor have they  reached out to me personally at any time  everything i am telling you concerning  their actions comes via four degrees of  separation where their team communicates  with the japanese youtube team who  communicates with the american youtube  team who communicates with my youtube  contact who then relays all of that info  back to me however time and again  youtube would encounter the same  pushback from toei who i presume see me  as no different than the people who  upload the dragon ball films in full on  youtube they see me as a pirate  and in short  it appears to be that toei doesn't  believe that there is an acceptable  application of their content online with  regards to fair use which is extremely  unfortunate as i believe similar to how  video games have embraced the online  sphere i sincerely believe that a  collaborative or symbiotic relationship  between online creators and copyright  owners is not only more than possible  but would likely work extremely well for  both sides if they were more open to it  and the way that they're going it's my  belief that it will only hurt both  parties perhaps more so than they  believe is possible and look this is  just my opinion but i genuinely believe  that had it not been for team four star  and their dragon ball z bridge series  dragon ball wouldn't have remained  nearly as popular in the western world  during the time where not much new  content surrounding the property was  being released and that's not to slight  the works or efforts of official sources  they do an incredible job but is to  speak to the opportunity that's being  left on the table perhaps without proper  consideration with all that said that  left me in a difficult position without  toei willing to budge on the matter if  they were to file a lawsuit in japan  then in a japanese court it's possible i  would have little chance due to the very  narrow application of their version of  fair use and this  is where youtube did something they have  never done before  a move that has added a brand new step  in their copyright policy or protocol  and while this is a policy youtube uses  in other legal removal areas it's the  very first time they're applying it to  copyright  okay so  a legal copyright removal has to  consider fair use or other copyright  exceptions right my videos are delivered  in english and clearly are targeted to  those in the western world and so  youtube removed the videos in japan  because given their limited application  of copyright exceptions toei might see  this as infringing in japan however  youtube felt the videos could reasonably  qualify for a fair use exemption in most  of the rest of the world so the content  will remain up everywhere else until or  unless toei can make an argument that it  would not qualify for copyright  exemption in other territories in short  since japan isn't a demographic i even  attempt to target and didn't have the  capability of abstaining from uploading  to in the past  youtube has elected to block my videos  in japan so that if they wish to block  those videos in the future they will  have to do so in a country outside of  japanese law thus giving me what i  believe to be a fair chance and well  that's where we are now following the  release of this video i will be making  public all of the videos that were once  blocked and only time will tell what the  future will hold for my channel and what  toei may or may not do  my hope is nothing but given how  unpredictable this entire situation has  been  who knows what might and as i've  mentioned very well can happen but  something i do want to say is that while  i am perfectly willing to and have  pointed out in the past shortcomings of  youtube as a platform and supporting its  creators i will also point out  experiences i've had where without them  i would have honestly been lost this is  such an occasion youtube isn't one  entity it's a massive group of people  that have all different opinions and  backgrounds i can't speak to the quality  of everyone working at youtube but i can  say that the people i've been in contact  with over the last month following my  going dark on social media  have been some of the kindest and most  eager to help people i've ever spoken to  that have expressed a genuine desire to  help me have worked tirelessly to help  me find a solution in this almost  impossible situation and perhaps most  importantly i think their heart is in  the right place again i cannot speak for  everyone's experience with youtube and  their respective personnel and i have  been very very vocal about their  shortcomings particularly in this  situation early on and i still think a  lot of work needs to be done to make  sure something like this doesn't happen  again people shouldn't need to create a  storm to get attention but i think it's  also important to champion the good that  they do when they do it and in this  situation they sincerely helped me  greatly

